==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|gem-pro|unþijō|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|unt-|lang=ang}}. Germanic cognates include Old Saxon [[uðia|ūðia]], Old High German [[undea]], Old Norse [[unnr]], [[uðr]]. The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin [[unda]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/yːθ/|lang=ang}}

